// PLAN-0471 T2.7 (user decision #5, 2026-10-09): explicit Oxfmt policy.
// Values are pinned to Oxfmt 0.68.0 RUNTIME defaults, verified by stdin probe
// and full-tree bisection (see plans/PLAN-0471-*/evidence/m2-t27-oxfmt.md):
// formatting must stay byte-identical to the pre-config state (zero drift).
// Notes from probing:
// - Runtime default tabWidth is 4 when NO config file exists, but drops to 2
//   once any .oxfmtrc exists — so tabWidth MUST be pinned explicitly.
// - Runtime default printWidth is 100 (matches schema doc).
// - Runtime default proseWrap is preserve; explicit "preserve" triggers
//   markdown list-blank-line normalization that the implicit default does
//   NOT do — so proseWrap must stay UNSET (keep implicit default).
// - Without a config file, Markdown files are not formatted at all; with a
//   config they get scanned. To keep zero drift, docs are excluded below.
// When upgrading Oxfmt: run `oxfmt --check .` and review any new drift
// before adopting the new version's defaults here.
{
    "ignorePatterns": ["AGENTS.md", "*.md"],
    "tabWidth": 4,
    "printWidth": 100,
}
